    {
      "name": "Hitchhiker Escape",
      "type": "Escape",
      "from": [
        "Armbar"
      ],
      "to": [
        "Bottom Side Control"
      ],
      "notes": "Roll over the trapped shoulder (the one opposite the leg crossing the neck) while hiding the elbow. Works best once the arm is extending - the attacker's commitment is what makes the roll available. The extension threat you are trading against is real, so commit fully. Lands in bottom side control if clean, recovers to guard if they release to avoid the roll."
    },
    {
      "name": "Roll-through to Standard Triangle",
      "type": "Transition",
      "from": [
        "Mounted Triangle"
      ],
      "to": [
        "Triangle"
      ],
      "notes": "Roll over the trapped shoulder. The lock stays; the position becomes a standard guard triangle. Finish is identical from there - you are not escaping, you are reconfiguring."
    },
